Package: cumulevel
Type: Package
Title: Weighted Causal Estimands for Cumulative Multilevel Exposures
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mohamed Raouf", "Benmakrelouf", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "ismtid_raouf@hotmail.fr",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2914-111X")),
    person("Abdelkader", "Tatachak", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4181-605X")))
Description: Estimation of a family of weighted causal estimands for exposures
    that are cumulative and hierarchical, such as educational attainment,
    disease stage or pack-years of tobacco, where attaining a level entails
    having attained all preceding ones. Dichotomising such an exposure
    silently attributes to the target level whatever happens above it. The
    package makes that attribution assumption an explicit parameter: a system
    of contribution weights indexes a family of estimands whose boundary
    members are the restricted average treatment effect and the binary
    average treatment effect. Estimation is by a level-specific weighted
    targeted minimum loss-based estimator that is doubly robust and
    semiparametrically efficient under cross-fitting, following Benmakrelouf
    and Tatachak (2026). Positivity diagnostics are reported by default, and
    a probabilistic sensitivity layer propagates attribution uncertainty
    jointly with sampling uncertainty. Includes NHANES 2005-2006 pack-years
    and linked mortality data as a worked example.
